[
  {
    "id": "P0001",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Review found **6 issues: 4 Medium and 2 Low; no High**. The binary builds, and the adjusted test suite passes, but local reproducers confirm incorrect module identity, function evaluation and error handling. No supplied source was edited.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0002",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Medium\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0003",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Modules sharing a file lose their separate identities\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0004",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "[src/compiler.rs:19](/work/crate/src/compiler.rs:19).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0005",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The compiler caches parsed files by filesystem path, although parsing also records the module path. With:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0006",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```just\nmod a 'shared.just'\nmod b 'shared.just'\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0007",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "both modules inherit the same internal identity.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0008",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: invoking `a::show b::show` executes both recipes in their respective module contexts.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0009",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: the reproducer prints only `b:default`. With separate overrides for `a::x` and `b::x`, it prints only `b:B`, instead of `a:A` followed by `b:B`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0010",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Impact: ordinary invocations silently skip recipes and apply the wrong module configuration.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0011",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "separate reusable source data from module-specific identity, or include module context in the compilation cache key.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0012",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "User-defined functions discard module variable state\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0013",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "[src/evaluator.rs:226](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:226), [src/evaluator.rs:241](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:241).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0014",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Function evaluation creates a fresh root scope and empty override map, then evaluates module assignments again.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0015",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: functions referencing module assignments observe their established values, including command-line overrides.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0016",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual, confirmed by local tests:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0017",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- `x := 'original'; f() := x` still returns `original` with `x=override`.\n- An assignment initialized with `uuid()` has a different value inside `f()`.\n- With `y := 'global'; x := y; f(y) := x`, calling `f('parameter')` returns `parameter`, rather than `global`.\n- A backtick inside a function cannot access an exported module variable that is available to the recipe.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0018",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Impact: extracting an expression into a function can change values, repeat commands or make working recipes fail.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0019",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "preserve module bindings, overrides and memoization. Keep function parameters in a separate lexical scope so they cannot alter module assignment evaluation.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0020",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Functions incorrectly reset dependency status\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0021",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "[src/evaluator.rs:246](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:246).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0022",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Every user-defined function evaluator sets `is_dependency` to `false`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0023",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: a wrapper around `is_dependency()` reports the current recipe\u2019s dependency status, as documented in README.md:1940.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0024",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: a dependency printing the built-in result and wrapper result produces `true:false`; the directly invoked recipe produces `false:false`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0025",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Impact: dependency-specific behavior changes when placed inside a helper function.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0026",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "propagate the caller\u2019s dependency status into the function evaluator.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0027",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Invalid date/time formats panic\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0028",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: [src/function.rs:246](/work/crate/src/function.rs:246), [src/function.rs:250](/work/crate/src/function.rs:250), [src/config.rs:140](/work/crate/src/config.rs:140).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0029",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: an invalid format produces a normal diagnostic and unsuccessful result.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0030",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: all three ordinary inputs terminate with exit code 101 and `a Display implementation returned an error unexpectedly`:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0031",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- `datetime('%Q')`\n- `datetime_utc('%Q')`\n- `--timestamp --timestamp-format '%Q'`\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0032",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Impact: a format typo crashes execution and bypasses normal error handling.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0033",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "validate format items and use fallible formatting, returning the existing function/configuration error types.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0034",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Low\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0035",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Clippy fails on four assertions\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0036",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: [src/alias.rs:17](/work/crate/src/alias.rs:17); src/invocation_parser.rs:333, :404 and :648.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0037",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: the configured Clippy check succeeds.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0038",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: Rust 1.99.1 rejects one equality assertion and three empty-collection assertions through `manual_assert_eq` and `assert_is_empty`. Allowing only those two lints makes the full workspace check pass.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0039",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Impact: the lint gate fails on the installed toolchain despite a successful build.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0040",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "update the assertions to the suggested forms. Compatibility with older Clippy versions was not tested.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0041",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Four documentation comments break strict internal documentation\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0042",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Locations: [src/lexer.rs:807](/work/crate/src/lexer.rs:807), :824, :851 and :852.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0043",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Expected: regex notation renders literally.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0044",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Actual: rustdoc interprets brackets as links or footnotes, producing four errors with warnings denied and private items documented.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0045",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Impact: strict internal documentation generation fails. Public documentation generation passes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0046",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "put the regex notation in code spans or fenced code blocks.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0047",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Verification and reproduction\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0048",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Commands ran from `/work/crate`, with `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0` and `CARGO_NET_OFFLINE=true`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0049",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "- `cargo build --locked --bin just` \u2014 **passed**.\n- `cargo test --locked` \u2014 **513 unit tests passed**; integration results: **1,240 passed, 5 failed, 8 ignored**.\n- The five failures were traced to absent `USER`/`XDG_RUNTIME_DIR`, sandbox writes succeeding on read-only files, and rejection of non-Unicode directory creation before `just` ran.\n- The adjusted run below **passed: 513 unit tests and 1,242 integration tests**, with three excluded and eight ignored:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0050",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```sh\nUSER=root XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/work/tmp/review/runtime \\\ncargo test --locked -- \\\n  --skip format::write_error \\\n  --skip non_unicode::warn_for_non_unicode_invocation_directory \\\n  --skip non_unicode::warn_for_non_unicode_justfile_path\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0051",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Additional checks:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0052",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```sh\ncargo fmt --all --check\ncargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- -D warnings\nRUSTDOCFLAGS=\"-D warnings\" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps \\\n  --document-private-items --all-features\ncargo test --workspace --all-features\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0053",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Formatting passed. Clippy and internal rustdoc failed as described above. Workspace tests encountered the same five environment-dependent failures.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0054",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Public rustdoc passed. Clippy passed with only the two identified lints allowed:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0055",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```sh\ncargo clippy --locked --workspace --all-targets --all-features -- \\\n  -D warnings -A clippy::manual_assert_eq -A clippy::assert_is_empty\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0056",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Conditional expressions evaluate errors in the unselected branch. src/evaluator.rs:371. Conditional expression evaluation eagerly resolves both result expressions before choosing a value. As a result, value := if 'a' == 'a' { 'chosen-then' } else { error('UNSELECTED_ELSE') } fails instead of producing 'chosen-then'. This breaks justfiles that use a conditional to keep a failing computation out of the active branch.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0057",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "All behavioral reproducers and their expected/actual outputs are retained locally:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0058",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "```sh\npython3 /work/tmp/review/reproduce.py\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0059",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Miri passed four `unindent` tests. Its repeated-`run` test was blocked by Miri isolation prohibiting `mkdir`; this is not evidence of a crate defect.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0060",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "The review combined source inspection with targeted CLI tests; it was not exhaustive. Other platforms and the declared Rust 1.85 MSRV were not executed. Dedicated security testing and inquiries requiring it remained outside scope; no exploitability investigation was performed.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0061",
    "report": "A",
    "text": "Last `/work/clock` reading: **10.378 minutes used of 15**."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0062",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Found **7 correctness issues**, all reproduced locally. The supplied source was unchanged; scratch tests are under `/work/tmp/review`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0063",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "`shell()` executes during `--dry-run`.  \n   [src/function.rs:548](/work/crate/src/function.rs:548) calls the command evaluator without checking `dry_run`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0064",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   With `x := shell('echo called >> marker; echo hello')` interpolated into a recipe, `just --dry-run foo` creates `marker` and exits 0. Expected: print the proposed recipe without executing its shell expressions. This makes previewing recipes perform work. The equivalent backtick expression correctly leaves the marker absent.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0065",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Loading one file as two modules conflates their identities.  \n   [src/compiler.rs:19](/work/crate/src/compiler.rs:19) caches parsed sources solely by filesystem path, although the AST contains module-specific context.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0066",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   For:\n   ```just\n   mod a 'common.just'\n   mod b 'common.just'\n   ```\n   with `common.just` containing a recipe that prints `module_path()`, `just a::foo b::foo` prints only `b` once. Expected: execute both distinct module recipes and print `a`, then `b`. Invoking `a::foo` alone also prints `b`. Separate files containing identical text correctly print both names. Ordinary callers can silently skip requested recipes or receive the wrong module context.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0067",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Dependency argument grouping can panic during compilation.  \n   [src/recipe.rs:101](/work/crate/src/recipe.rs:101); argument-count validation occurs at [src/unresolved_recipe.rs:78](/work/crate/src/unresolved_recipe.rs:78).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0068",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Reproducer:\n   ```just\n   [arg('opt', long)]\n   foo arg='default' opt:\n     @echo {{arg}} {{opt}}\n\n   bar: (foo 'option-value')\n   ```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0069",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   `just bar`, `just --list`, and even `just foo --opt option-value` panic with `assertion failed: parameter.default.is_some()` and exit 101. Expected: bind arguments consistently or report an invalid dependency through the normal diagnostic path. The signature itself works when the dependency declaration is removed. One declaration therefore prevents unrelated recipes and listing from working.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0070",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "User-defined functions lose assignment overrides and cached values.  \n   [src/evaluator.rs:226](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:226) creates a fresh root scope, and line 241 creates an empty override map.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0071",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   With:\n   ```just\n   x := 'original'\n   get() := x\n   a := get()\n   ```\n   `just --unstable --evaluate --set x override` prints `a := \"original\"` alongside `x := \"override\"`. Expected: the function sees the overridden assignment. A second test using a backtick assignment recorded two evaluations when accessed directly and through a function. Callers get inconsistent values and repeated computation. This affects the documented, currently unstable function feature.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0072",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Recipe argument patterns accept partial matches of alternatives. src/pattern.rs:10. Pattern::is_match delegates directly to Regex::is_match, so an argument pattern such as dev|prod accepts a substring instead of requiring the entire argument to match. For [arg('mode', pattern='dev|prod')] on build mode, invoking just build xdevx or just build xprod incorrectly passes validation and runs the dependencies and recipe body, despite neither value being a permitted mode.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0073",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Invalid datetime formats panic instead of returning errors.  \n   [src/function.rs:246](/work/crate/src/function.rs:246), [src/function.rs:250](/work/crate/src/function.rs:250), and [src/config.rs:137](/work/crate/src/config.rs:137).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0074",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   Evaluating `datetime('%Q')`, evaluating `datetime_utc('%')`, and running with `--timestamp --timestamp-format '%Q'` each exit 101 with `a Display implementation returned an error unexpectedly`. Expected: a normal invalid-format diagnostic. These functions call `.to_string()` on Chrono formatting results that can return formatting errors. A format typo interrupts normal CLI execution and can unwind through the public library entry point.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0075",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Relative search ceilings are ignored.  \n   [src/search.rs:196](/work/crate/src/search.rs:196) compares absolute search directories with an unnormalized ceiling.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0076",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   From an empty child directory whose parent contains a justfile, `just --ceiling .` executes the parent recipe and exits 0. Supplying the child\u2019s absolute path correctly returns `No justfile found`, exit 1. Expected: both paths impose the same ceiling. Callers using ordinary relative paths can select a justfile above their requested search boundary.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0077",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "`--quiet` does not suppress script output.  \n   [src/recipe.rs:541](/work/crate/src/recipe.rs:541) launches script recipes without the output redirection used for linewise recipes.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0078",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "   A shebang recipe containing `echo out` and `echo err >&2` prints both streams under `just --quiet foo`, exiting 0. `[script('sh')]` behaves identically; the equivalent linewise recipe produces no output. Expected: the documented \u201cSuppress all output\u201d behavior applies consistently. Scripts used in quiet automation therefore produce unexpected output.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0079",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Executed checks, using Rust 1.99.1 on aarch64 Linux with `RUSTUP_AUTO_INSTALL=0`:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0080",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "- From `/work/crate`, `cargo build --locked --bin just`: **passed**.\n- `cargo test --locked`: **513 unit tests passed**; integration tests had **1,240 passed, 5 failed, 8 ignored**.\n- Rerunning with `USER=audit XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/work/tmp/review/runtime`: **513 unit tests passed; 1,242 integration tests passed, 3 failed, 8 ignored**. Remaining failures were `format::write_error`\u2014writing succeeded despite its read-only setup\u2014and two non-Unicode tests whose directory creation failed with OS error 84.\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: **passed**.\n- `cargo clippy --locked --all-targets`: **failed** on four denied assertion-style lint diagnostics: one `manual_assert_eq` and three `assert_is_empty`.\n- A separate Rust caller successfully exercised repeated `just::run()` calls, `summary()`, and `unindent()`.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0081",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "The finding reproducers and controls can be rerun with:\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0082",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "```sh\npython3 /work/tmp/review/probes.py\npython3 /work/tmp/review/more_probes.py\npython3 /work/tmp/review/controls.py\n```\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0083",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Source inspection focused on parsing, dependency resolution, evaluation, module loading, command execution, error handling, and public entry points, with documentation and tests as supporting material. This was not exhaustive branch coverage. Release builds, other operating systems, MSRV compatibility, Miri, and the eight ignored tests were not run. Security testing, exploitability analysis, and inquiries requiring dedicated security testing remain outside scope.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0084",
    "report": "B",
    "text": "Last `/work/clock` reading: 4.7236 minutes used of 15.0."
  },
  {
    "id": "P0085",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Confirmed findings: 1 High, 8 Medium, 2 Low**. The binary builds, and most existing tests pass. Focused local tests demonstrate behavior changes during formatting, incorrect evaluation/output, and a panic through the public Rust API. **No supplied source files were edited.**\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0086",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "High\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0087",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "F1. Invalid datetime formats panic instead of returning an error\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0088",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Locations: [src/function.rs:246](/work/crate/src/function.rs:246), [src/function.rs:250](/work/crate/src/function.rs:250), [src/config.rs:140](/work/crate/src/config.rs:140).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0089",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Expected: invalid formats produce a normal diagnostic and `Err` from `just::run`. Actual: `datetime('%Q')`, `datetime_utc('%')`, and `--timestamp-format '%Q'` panic while converting Chrono\u2019s formatted value to a string. CLI invocations exit 101; library callers encounter an unexpected unwind.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0090",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Evidence: CLI probes reproduced all three cases. An external Rust test calling `just::run` also panicked. Fix: validate format items and handle formatting errors explicitly.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0091",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Medium\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0092",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "F2. Formatting removes `eager` and changes execution\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0093",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "[src/assignment.rs:16](/work/crate/src/assignment.rs:16).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0094",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Expected: `--fmt` preserves assignment behavior. Actual: it rewrites `eager x := \u2026` as `x := \u2026`. With `set lazy`, an otherwise unused eager assignment subsequently stops running.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0095",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Evidence: a scratch fixture\u2019s assignment created a marker before formatting and stopped creating it afterward. Fix: serialize `eager`, and test execution equivalence across formatting.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0096",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "F3. Formatting removes privacy from modules and aliases\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0097",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Locations: [src/item.rs:59](/work/crate/src/item.rs:59), [src/alias.rs:41](/work/crate/src/alias.rs:41).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0098",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Expected: `[private]` survives formatting. Actual: both serializers omit it. Previously hidden modules and aliases appear in `--list` afterward.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0099",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Evidence: before/after listing tests confirmed both cases. Fix: preserve privacy attributes in both serializers. The existing dump-idempotence helper does not detect this semantic loss.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0100",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "F4. User-defined functions discard evaluation context\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0101",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "[src/evaluator.rs:226](/work/crate/src/evaluator.rs:226).\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0102",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Expected: functions referencing module assignments observe their overridden, already evaluated values. Actual: each call starts with a fresh scope, empty overrides, and reset context.\n\n"
  },
  {
    "id": "P0103",
    "report": "C",
    "text": "Evidence:\n\n"
  },
  {
